# Line endings for files that run on Linux servers.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which stores LF
# in git and checks out CRLF locally. That works only as long as every
# contributor has the same setting. If a shell script is ever committed with
# CRLF, Linux reads the shebang as "#!/bin/bash\r" and the Pterodactyl server
# fails to boot with a bare "no such file or directory" that points at
# nothing obvious.
#
# Pinning eol=lf on the files that Linux executes or parses removes that
# dependency on local git configuration.

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
.Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Binaries git must not touch.
*.jar   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.gif   binary
*.pkl   binary
